The '''Flooded Caves''' is one of the environments in [[chapter 2]] added in ''[[The Binding of Isaac: Afterbirth]]''. The theme of the Flooded Caves is water; as such, most of the enemies inhabiting it are airborne, such as One Tooth and flies, and many of them shoot projectiles, while there are fewer ground-bound and contact-damage-reliant enemies. Some enemies like the {{e|Hive}} have a chance to be replaced with their drowned variants {{dlc|nr}} and rocks have a chance to be replaced with water-filled pits.

The Flooded Cave's alternate floors are the {{s|Caves}} and the {{s|Catacombs}}.

{{dlc+|r}}After {{a|A Secret Exit}} is unlocked, a boarded door similar to the one leading to a [[Bedroom]] will appear in this floor's {{r|Boss Room}} upon defeating the boss, leading to the {{S|Mines}} / {{S|Ashpit}}. This door, like a Bedroom, requires two bombs to be opened. Unlike {{r|Angel Room}}s and {{r|Devil Room}}s, this door never disappears.{{dlc-}}

{{dlc+|r}} Though there is some overlap with {{s|Downpour}} due to both featuring water flooding, Downpour's unique enemies are often ghostly and supernatural in nature as opposed to the Flooded Cave's theme of drowned or bloated enemies.{{dlc-}}

{{dlc|a+}} The Flooded Caves are unlocked by defeating {{e|It Lives!}} 16 times.
* {{dlc+|r}} Killing {{e|Dogma}} and {{e|The Beast}} also increases this tally, as does {{s|Mausoleum}}'s version of {{e|Mom's Heart}}.{{dlc-}}

